1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,740
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

2
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:12,240
 Good morning, brothers and sisters.

3
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:14,800
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

4
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:17,520
 Happy Father's Day.

5
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:26,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

6
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:27,800
 Some of you may remember what it was

7
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:32,080
 like to have your dad hold your hand when you cross the road.

8
00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:33,520
 That's a child.

9
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:40,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

10
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:43,120
 And that is kind of like a big hand wrapping entirely

11
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:44,440
 around your little hands.

12
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:46,760
 And you had nothing to fear, because you know

13
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:50,120
 that he would never let go.

14
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:54,400
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

15
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:56,680
 But not everyone have warm memories when

16
00:00:56,680 --> 00:00:58,800
 it comes to their father's hand.

17
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:02,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

18
00:01:02,120 --> 00:01:05,080
 Some remember a hand that was never present.

19
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:09,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

20
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:11,880
 Others remember the hands that would lash out or even hurt

21
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:12,400
 others.

22
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:18,200
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

23
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,480
 And for some of us, what they miss the most on these Father's

24
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:24,320
 Days is a hand that they can no longer hold.

25
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:30,520
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

26
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:32,960
 So our passage today is short, just four verses,

27
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:35,600
 but the word "hands" here appears twice.

28
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:43,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

29
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:44,480
 And through this verse, Jesus wants

30
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:47,600
 to reveal to us what kind of Father our Heavenly Father is.

31
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:49,880
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

32
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:51,880
 And what kind of hands he has.

33
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:55,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

34
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:57,840
 And by the end of the sermon, we will know these three things.

35
00:01:57,840 --> 00:02:00,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

36
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:02,880
 First, whose hands does the Father's hold?

37
00:02:02,880 --> 00:02:08,880
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

38
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:10,840
 And second, why does Jesus say that no one

39
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:13,160
 is able to snatch them out of the Father's hand?

40
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:18,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

41
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:21,040
 And third, what does the phrase "I and the Father are one"

42
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:22,640
 have to do with Father's Day?

43
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:25,440
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

44
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:27,840
 If you're ready, we'll read our passage today.

45
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:48,720
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

46
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:50,720
 My sheep hear my voice, and I know them,

47
00:02:50,720 --> 00:02:52,040
 and they follow me.

48
00:02:52,040 --> 00:02:54,800
 I give them eternal life, and they will never perish.

49
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:57,440
 And no one will snatch them out of my hand.

50
00:02:57,440 --> 00:03:00,880
 My Father, who has given them to me, is greater than all.

51
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:04,280
 And no one is able to snatch them out of the Father's hand.

52
00:03:04,280 --> 00:03:06,640
 I and the Father are one.

53
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:10,960
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

54
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:12,400
 So let's first look at the context

55
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,960
 in which Jesus gave these words.

56
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:18,960
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

57
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:22,440
 Verse 22 tells us that it was the festival of dedication

58
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:23,440
 during the wintertime.

59
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:35,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

60
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:36,840
 So the festival of dedication actually

61
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:40,360
 commemorates the Maccabean-era purification of the temple,

62
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:43,040
 when the temple, defiled by a foreign king,

63
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:46,400
 was rededicated as holy to the Lord.

64
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:56,200
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

65
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:58,480
 And it was at this festival that a group of Jews

66
00:03:58,480 --> 00:04:00,640
 surrounded Jesus and demanded him,

67
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:02,600
 how long will you keep us guessing?

68
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:05,760
 If you're the Christ, just tell us plainly.

69
00:04:05,760 --> 00:04:09,960
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

70
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:13,120
 Jesus did not answer them directly with I am or I'm not.

71
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:15,160
 Instead, he spoke about sheep.

72
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:17,880
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

73
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:20,160
 And this raises our first question today.

74
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:29,320
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

75
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:31,960
 So why didn't Jesus simply answer them yes or no

76
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:34,040
 to the are you the Christ questions?

77
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:37,120
 But instead, he spoke of my sheep hear my voice.

78
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:46,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

79
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:47,680
 In fact, his very way of answering it

80
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:49,800
 is in and of itself the answer.

81
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:52,560
 So let us follow the passage questions by questions,

82
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:53,720
 beginning with the first one.

83
00:04:53,720 --> 00:05:01,400
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

84
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:03,840
 Jesus' answer to the questions, are you the Christ,

85
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:07,080
 was not a theological argument, but a description

86
00:05:07,080 --> 00:05:08,440
 of a relationship.

87
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:14,600
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

88
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:17,000
 The three verbs in verse 27 are beautiful.

89
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:21,360
 The sheep hear my voice, I know them, and they follow me.

90
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:28,280
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

91
00:05:28,280 --> 00:05:31,160
 In the original language, hear is not just

92
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:34,960
 mere physical hearing, but discerning and hearing.

93
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:39,960
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

94
00:05:39,960 --> 00:05:42,400
 Like a child in a crowd that instantly recognized

95
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:43,760
 their father's voice.

96
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:49,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

97
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:52,320
 And know is not just knowing some facts about someone,

98
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:55,120
 but a deep knowing found in relationship.

99
00:05:55,120 --> 00:06:02,280
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

100
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:05,000
 So Jesus already said in verse 14 and 15,

101
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,240
 I know my sheep, and my sheep know me,

102
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:10,000
 just as the father knows me, and I know the father.

103
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:15,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

104
00:06:15,760 --> 00:06:17,720
 In other words, the knowing between the sheep

105
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:19,480
 and the shepherd is actually rooted

106
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:22,240
 in the knowing between the father and the son.

107
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:27,160
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

108
00:06:27,160 --> 00:06:30,440
 We are known by God because of the deep mutual knowing that

109
00:06:30,440 --> 00:06:33,480
 has already exists between the father and the son.

110
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:41,000
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

111
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,320
 And now, once we recognize who the shepherd is,

112
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:44,920
 the second questions follow.

113
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:47,240
 How does this shepherd keep his sheep?

114
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:51,680
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

115
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:53,640
 And why does the word "hen" appear twice

116
00:06:53,640 --> 00:06:55,240
 in such a short passage?

117
00:06:55,240 --> 00:07:05,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

118
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:08,040
 So let us begin from the climax here in verse 28.

119
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:11,160
 "I give them eternal life, and they will never perish,

120
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:13,840
 and no one will snatch them out of my hand."

121
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:15,520
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

122
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:17,560
 So two words here, no forwarding.

123
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:25,880
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH] First, "will never perish"

124
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:28,800
 is a double negative, an emphatic expression

125
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:32,080
 meaning absolutely forever, they will not perish.

126
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:42,000
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

127
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,720
 Second, "snatch," the word, is the same word

128
00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:48,080
 used in verse 12, describing a wolf seizing the sheep

129
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:49,520
 and scattering the flock.

130
00:07:49,520 --> 00:07:56,000
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

131
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,840
 In other words, Jesus is not saying that there is no danger

132
00:07:58,840 --> 00:08:00,880
 or no fierce wolf.

133
00:08:00,880 --> 00:08:05,200
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

134
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:08,400
 What he's saying is no matter how great the wolf power is,

135
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:09,880
 it cannot seize them.

136
00:08:09,880 --> 00:08:16,920
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

137
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:17,840
 Then notice this.

138
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:20,360
 In verse 28, it says, "out of my hand."

139
00:08:20,360 --> 00:08:23,120
 And verse 29, it says, "out of the Father's hands."

140
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:29,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

141
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:31,440
 Why does Jesus have to say the same thing twice,

142
00:08:31,440 --> 00:08:35,200
 once using my hand and the other time using the Father's hand?

143
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:39,240
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

144
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:41,200
 The answer can be found in verse 30.

145
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:43,320
 I and the Father are one.

146
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:47,840
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

147
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:50,080
 This is not two hands in the tug of war.

148
00:08:50,080 --> 00:08:52,920
 It is the same grip and the same power.

149
00:08:52,920 --> 00:08:57,360
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

150
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:59,000
 The sheep held in the son's hands

151
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:01,240
 are also held in the Father's hand.

152
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:04,720
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

153
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:08,360
 This is a double assurance, and yet it is the same hand.

154
00:09:08,360 --> 00:09:14,320
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

155
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:17,000
 And verse 29, it has a crucial phase,

156
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,920
 that this hand is greater than all.

157
00:09:18,920 --> 00:09:21,960
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

158
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:23,920
 This leads us to the first misconception

159
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:25,560
 that we need to address.

160
00:09:25,560 --> 00:09:27,640
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

161
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:29,200
 Many people live an exhausting life,

162
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:30,440
 even after they come to faith.

163
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:34,160
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

164
00:09:34,160 --> 00:09:35,680
 Because they think that salvation

165
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:37,960
 is like a game of holding on to the Father's hand.

166
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:42,160
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

167
00:09:42,160 --> 00:09:45,440
 The moment they loosen the grip, or grow weak, or stumble,

168
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:47,320
 they will fall and lose their salvation.

169
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:50,640
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

170
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:53,680
 So they live in constant fear that they are not

171
00:09:53,680 --> 00:09:55,720
 holding tight enough.

172
00:09:55,720 --> 00:10:03,320
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

173
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:06,760
 But if we look at our passage from verse 27 to 30,

174
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:08,560
 none of the verses says that the sheep

175
00:10:08,560 --> 00:10:10,280
 must hold on to their shepherd.

176
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:15,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

177
00:10:15,760 --> 00:10:17,160
 From the beginning to the end, it

178
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:19,880
 is always the shepherd's hand that holds the sheep.

179
00:10:19,880 --> 00:10:22,120
 It is the Father's hand that holds the sheep.

180
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:26,400
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

181
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:29,680
 Return to the earlier image that a child crossing the street

182
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:31,080
 is safe.

183
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:34,600
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

184
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:36,800
 Not because he grips his father's hand with all

185
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:37,520
 his strength.

186
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:41,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

187
00:10:41,040 --> 00:10:43,240
 But because of his father's hands that wraps around

188
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:44,640
 the little one entirely.

189
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:47,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

190
00:10:47,760 --> 00:10:50,800
 Even if the child lets go, the father does not.

191
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:58,200
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

192
00:10:58,200 --> 00:11:01,240
 Your salvation does not depend on how tightly you hold on to.

193
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:03,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

194
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:05,920
 And that hand is greater than all.

195
00:11:05,920 --> 00:11:12,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

196
00:11:12,760 --> 00:11:15,240
 Finally, we come to the weightiest statement here,

197
00:11:15,240 --> 00:11:18,920
 which brings up the third and final question.

198
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:23,840
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

199
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:26,000
 What does the word "one" mean when Jesus says,

200
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,480
 "I and the Father are one"?

201
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:31,560
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

202
00:11:31,560 --> 00:11:33,560
 The word "one" here in the original Greek

203
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:39,000
 is "neuter," not "masculine" or "not masculine."

204
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:45,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

205
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:47,480
 This grammatical distinction is important

206
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:50,160
 because Jesus is not saying that the Father and the Son

207
00:11:50,160 --> 00:11:51,360
 are the same person.

208
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:57,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

209
00:11:57,480 --> 00:11:59,400
 What he's saying is that the Father and the Son

210
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:03,440
 are completely one in nature, in will, in action, and power.

211
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:09,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

212
00:12:09,080 --> 00:12:12,800
 They are two distinct persons, yet one God, one will,

213
00:12:12,800 --> 00:12:13,960
 and one hand.

214
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:16,440
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

215
00:12:16,440 --> 00:12:18,600
 This addressed our second misconception.

216
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:23,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

217
00:12:23,760 --> 00:12:25,240
 "I and the Father are one" does not

218
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:28,360
 mean that Jesus and the Father are indistinguishable.

219
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:35,960
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

220
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:38,280
 And the Jewish crowd, they actually understood exactly

221
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:40,760
 what Jesus meant, which is why in the next verse,

222
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:42,280
 they immediately pick up the stones

223
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:43,360
 and trying to stone Jesus.

224
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:48,880
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

225
00:12:48,880 --> 00:12:52,160
 And the reason is because Jesus claims that he, a mere man,

226
00:12:52,160 --> 00:12:53,480
 claimed to be God.

227
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:58,360
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

228
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:01,960
 Jesus was declaring, I am one with the Father in essence,

229
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:05,040
 will, and work, and what I do is what the Father does.

230
00:13:05,040 --> 00:13:12,280
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

231
00:13:12,280 --> 00:13:14,280
 It is precisely because the Son and the Father

232
00:13:14,280 --> 00:13:16,440
 are one that Jesus would later say,

233
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:19,400
 "Whoever has seen the Father has seen me.

234
00:13:19,400 --> 00:13:22,000
 Whoever has seen me has seen the Father."

235
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:25,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

236
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:27,800
 And this is the most important statement for Father's Day

237
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:28,300
 today.

238
00:13:28,300 --> 00:13:31,240
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

239
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:34,480
 If we want to know what kind of Father our Heavenly Father is--

240
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:36,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

241
00:13:36,480 --> 00:13:37,600
 We don't have to guess.

242
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:39,520
 We simply look at Jesus.

243
00:13:39,520 --> 00:13:44,240
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

244
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:46,360
 Look at how Jesus treats his sheep,

245
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:48,360
 knowing them, giving them eternal life,

246
00:13:48,360 --> 00:13:49,520
 and never letting go.

247
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:51,400
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

248
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:53,880
 And that is what our Heavenly Father is like.

249
00:13:53,880 --> 00:14:00,360
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

250
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:02,480
 In fact, the setting of these words being spoken

251
00:14:02,480 --> 00:14:08,160
 on the festival of dedication make it even more wonderful.

252
00:14:08,160 --> 00:14:14,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

253
00:14:14,040 --> 00:14:16,480
 This festival commemorates the rededication,

254
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:18,920
 making holy again what has been defiled.

255
00:14:18,920 --> 00:14:26,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

256
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:28,400
 And in verse 36, Jesus described himself

257
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:31,640
 as the one whom the Father consecrated and sent

258
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:32,320
 into the world.

259
00:14:32,320 --> 00:14:35,280
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

260
00:14:35,280 --> 00:14:38,560
 Jesus reveals himself as the truly consecrated one.

261
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:44,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

262
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:46,600
 He came to bring back the loss and the woundership

263
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:49,120
 into the Father's hand.

264
00:14:49,120 --> 00:14:58,680
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

265
00:14:58,680 --> 00:15:01,440
 So in response to this Heavenly Father who is greater than all

266
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:05,200
 and never lets go, how might we respond to this Father's day?

267
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:13,280
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

268
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:15,920
 First, if the word "Father" brings you grief,

269
00:15:15,920 --> 00:15:19,400
 let the Heavenly Father redefine what "Fathers" mean.

270
00:15:19,400 --> 00:15:25,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

271
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:28,280
 We naturally project our image of an earthly father

272
00:15:28,280 --> 00:15:30,360
 onto our Heavenly Father sometimes.

273
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:34,960
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

274
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:36,760
 If your father was absent, you may

275
00:15:36,760 --> 00:15:39,960
 feel that God is also distant and would abandon you.

276
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:45,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

277
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:47,800
 And if your father was harsh or frightening,

278
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:51,000
 you may feel that God is always ready to punish you as well.

279
00:15:51,000 --> 00:16:01,240
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

280
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:03,560
 But when Jesus says, "I and the Father are one,"

281
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:04,640
 it means this.

282
00:16:04,640 --> 00:16:06,200
 To know the Heavenly Father, you don't

283
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:10,000
 have to guess through the lens of your earthly father, who

284
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:13,920
 disappoint you, but instead look through Jesus.

285
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:15,960
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

286
00:16:15,960 --> 00:16:19,240
 However Jesus treats you is how the Heavenly Father treats you.

287
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:25,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

288
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:28,320
 This week, find some quiet time to bring a disappointment

289
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:30,520
 and your wounds from your earthly father

290
00:16:30,520 --> 00:16:32,800
 before the Heavenly Father.

291
00:16:32,800 --> 00:16:37,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

292
00:16:37,120 --> 00:16:40,360
 And you can ask him to heal your understanding of the word "Father"

293
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:44,000
 through the image of Jesus.

294
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:50,640
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

295
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:52,840
 And this is Ken's testimony.

296
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:55,040
 So my father was an absent father.

297
00:16:55,040 --> 00:16:56,480
 From a very young age, he was not

298
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:59,760
 there for many of the important moments in my life.

299
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:04,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

300
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:07,520
 Whether it was the secondary school graduation, university,

301
00:17:07,520 --> 00:17:12,000
 or even post-graduation ceremony, he never showed up.

302
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:19,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

303
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:23,160
 Every time, I desperately hoped that he would appear and say,

304
00:17:23,160 --> 00:17:24,160
 "You did well.

305
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:26,760
 I'm so proud of you."

306
00:17:26,760 --> 00:17:33,280
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

307
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:35,640
 When I came to faith, I thought that this pain

308
00:17:35,640 --> 00:17:38,200
 would just naturally go away.

309
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:42,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

310
00:17:42,080 --> 00:17:44,920
 But then I discovered that this sense of not being a firm

311
00:17:44,920 --> 00:17:47,800
 can be projected onto the Heavenly Father.

312
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:57,600
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

313
00:17:57,600 --> 00:18:00,480
 Deep down in me, I felt that I was never doing enough,

314
00:18:00,480 --> 00:18:03,200
 that I have to keep striving to earn the Heavenly Father's

315
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:04,400
 approval.

316
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:10,920
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

317
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:13,880
 It was only until later when the Heavenly Father healed me

318
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:17,200
 and helped me to redefine things through Jesus.

319
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:22,560
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

320
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:24,840
 And he showed me how deeply I'm loved.

321
00:18:24,840 --> 00:18:26,920
 And I slowly move out from under the shadow

322
00:18:26,920 --> 00:18:28,760
 of not being reassured.

323
00:18:28,760 --> 00:18:38,920
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

324
00:18:38,920 --> 00:18:41,520
 So I would like to encourage everyone to do the same,

325
00:18:41,520 --> 00:18:43,320
 to bring your disappointments and wounds

326
00:18:43,320 --> 00:18:45,400
 about your earthly father honestly

327
00:18:45,400 --> 00:18:47,000
 before your Heavenly Father.

328
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:52,880
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

329
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:55,160
 And ask him to heal your understanding of the word

330
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:58,280
 "father" through the image of Jesus.

331
00:18:58,280 --> 00:19:05,280
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

332
00:19:05,280 --> 00:19:08,080
 Second, if you're longing for a hand that you can no longer

333
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:09,840
 hold, his father say--

334
00:19:09,840 --> 00:19:14,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

335
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:17,080
 Remember that your father is in our Heavenly Father's hand.

336
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:20,680
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

337
00:19:20,680 --> 00:19:23,240
 The scripture says no one is able to snatch them

338
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:24,680
 from the father's hand.

339
00:19:24,680 --> 00:19:27,680
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

340
00:19:27,680 --> 00:19:30,320
 If the father that you're missing belongs to the Lord--

341
00:19:30,320 --> 00:19:35,560
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

342
00:19:35,560 --> 00:19:37,280
 Then this is the promise for you.

343
00:19:37,280 --> 00:19:40,760
 Not even death can snatch him from the Heavenly Father's hand.

344
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:46,920
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

345
00:19:46,920 --> 00:19:49,040
 Third, if you are a father today,

346
00:19:49,040 --> 00:19:52,720
 ask the Lord to help us and learn to be like him.

347
00:19:52,720 --> 00:20:01,240
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

348
00:20:01,240 --> 00:20:03,320
 None of us as fathers are perfect.

349
00:20:03,320 --> 00:20:06,720
 We fail, we lose our temper, our absence,

350
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:08,080
 and we disappoint our children.

351
00:20:08,080 --> 00:20:18,680
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

352
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:20,640
 But our Heavenly Father has given us

353
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:23,720
 a model to follow, to truly know your children,

354
00:20:23,720 --> 00:20:27,880
 not just the greats, but to truly know them, to hold them,

355
00:20:27,880 --> 00:20:30,280
 and to not easily let go.

356
00:20:30,280 --> 00:20:36,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

357
00:20:36,120 --> 00:20:39,520
 You don't need to be a perfect father, but through the Lord,

358
00:20:39,520 --> 00:20:42,720
 you can be a father who never lets go.

359
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:47,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

360
00:20:47,760 --> 00:20:50,760
 The kind of father who, even when your children stumble,

361
00:20:50,760 --> 00:20:53,600
 or grow weak, or disappoint you, that you still

362
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:54,880
 don't release that hand.

363
00:20:54,880 --> 00:20:57,720
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

364
00:20:57,720 --> 00:21:00,640
 Because this is exactly what the Heavenly Father has always

365
00:21:00,640 --> 00:21:03,880
 done for us.

366
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:07,880
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

367
00:21:07,880 --> 00:21:10,680
 So let's return to the questions that we have at the beginning

368
00:21:10,680 --> 00:21:12,480
 and answer them together.

369
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:27,200
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

370
00:21:27,200 --> 00:21:30,440
 So first question, whose hand does the father hold?

371
00:21:30,440 --> 00:21:33,800
 He holds every sheep that hears his voice and follows him,

372
00:21:33,800 --> 00:21:37,040
 not because the sheep is good enough or hold tightly enough,

373
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:40,360
 but because the shepherd knows and has chosen that sheep.

374
00:21:40,360 --> 00:21:48,520
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

375
00:21:48,520 --> 00:21:51,200
 Second, what is the basis of our security?

376
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:53,960
 It is not on how tightly we hold on to,

377
00:21:53,960 --> 00:21:56,200
 but in a hand that is greater than all,

378
00:21:56,200 --> 00:21:58,920
 that no one can snatch us away from.

379
00:21:58,920 --> 00:22:12,600
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

380
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:14,920
 And third, what does I and the father are one

381
00:22:14,920 --> 00:22:17,040
 have to do with Father's Day?

382
00:22:17,040 --> 00:22:19,560
 It is because the son and the father are one

383
00:22:19,560 --> 00:22:22,000
 that we see the Heavenly Father's heart clearly

384
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:24,920
 through Jesus, a father who never lets go.

385
00:22:27,520 --> 00:22:40,560
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

386
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:43,040
 So some questions for us to reflect on.

387
00:22:43,040 --> 00:22:44,920
 When you hear the word "father," what

388
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:47,760
 is the first thing that comes to your heart?

389
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:49,880
 Has that feeling quietly shaped how you

390
00:22:49,880 --> 00:22:52,280
 understand our Heavenly Father?

391
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:58,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

392
00:22:58,120 --> 00:23:00,000
 And on this Father's Day, are you

393
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:03,240
 willing to let the Heavenly Father hold you again

394
00:23:03,240 --> 00:23:06,280
 through the image of Jesus?

395
00:23:06,280 --> 00:23:07,600
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

396
00:23:07,600 --> 00:23:10,760
 Let's pray together.

397
00:23:10,760 --> 00:23:17,400
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

398
00:23:17,400 --> 00:23:20,760
 Dear Heavenly Father, thank you for revealing to us

399
00:23:20,760 --> 00:23:24,640
 what kind of father you are through your son, Jesus.

400
00:23:24,640 --> 00:23:28,920
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

401
00:23:28,920 --> 00:23:32,480
 We thank you that you are not a father who is far off or cold

402
00:23:32,480 --> 00:23:34,760
 or always ready to punish us.

403
00:23:34,760 --> 00:23:39,960
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

404
00:23:39,960 --> 00:23:43,800
 But you are a father who knows us, who comes to find us,

405
00:23:43,800 --> 00:23:46,320
 who holds us with a hand greater than all.

406
00:23:46,320 --> 00:23:57,520
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

407
00:23:57,520 --> 00:23:59,840
 May you heal every wound from our earthly father

408
00:23:59,840 --> 00:24:01,120
 that we carry.

409
00:24:01,120 --> 00:24:03,600
 And may those who have been hurt by their fathers

410
00:24:03,600 --> 00:24:05,880
 or those who are missing their fathers today

411
00:24:05,880 --> 00:24:07,680
 be held anew by your hand.

412
00:24:07,680 --> 00:24:13,680
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

413
00:24:13,680 --> 00:24:17,120
 And may you help every father among us to learn from your

414
00:24:17,120 --> 00:24:20,080
 hands the one that never lets go.

415
00:24:20,080 --> 00:24:24,320
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

416
00:24:24,320 --> 00:24:26,200
 We give this Father's Day into your hands.

417
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:27,640
 In Jesus' name, we pray.

418
00:24:27,640 --> 00:24:28,160
 Amen.

419
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:29,600
 Amen.

420
00:24:29,600 --> 00:24:32,520
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

421
00:24:32,520 --> 00:24:36,200
 We wish you all a wonderful Father's Day.

